# Code owners
#
# GitHub asks the owner of a path for a review when a pull request changes it.
# With the branch protection rule "Require review from Code Owners" the pull
# request cannot be merged without that review.
#
# The difference list of the golden tests (docs/run-testing.md): a row is an
# accepted difference between the recorded behaviour and today's. An owner
# signs a row by approving the pull request that adds the signature;
# scripts/check-difference-signatures.js fails a signature without that review.
# Two owners are named because GitHub does not let the author of a pull request
# approve it: a pull request opened by one owner is signed by the other.
# The check reads the owner from this file on the target branch.
/server/tests/golden/differences.json @manzked @Intradmin
/.github/CODEOWNERS @manzked @Intradmin

# The gate runs on `pull_request`, so it runs the pull request's own copy of
# the workflow and of the two checks. Whoever can change one of them can switch
# the gate off, so each has the same owner as the list: the signature check, the
# check that a test-only pull request changes no production code, the workflow
# with the job "Golden difference list", and the check that every changed golden
# is named by a row. This only holds with the branch protection
# rule "Require review from Code Owners" on the target branch.
/scripts/check-difference-signatures.js @manzked @Intradmin
/scripts/check-test-only-diff.js @manzked @Intradmin
/.github/workflows/e2e.yml @manzked @Intradmin
